WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.667
(gentle instrumental music)

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:06.330
- [Narrator] Most cathedrals have been

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:11.160
built to withstand the test
of time, but not this one.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.630
Welcome to the Easter
Arches of Sicily, Italy.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.083
But come quick, they won't last.

00:00:26.444 --> 00:00:30.420
Every Easter, the town of
San Biagio in Sicily, Italy,

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.100
is home to a cathedral made out

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.490
of breads, cereals, and pastas.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:38.500
Visitors are able to wander
through the Arches of Bread

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.003
and enjoy the detailed designs up close.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.400
The structure is created by locals,

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.843
and takes around three
months to construct.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.940
The origins of this tradition date back

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.420
to ancient times when visiting royals

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.183
expected to be greeted
with grand displays.

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:00.420
San Biagio was a town
of mostly poor farmers,

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:03.123
so they used what they had: bread.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:07.330
In the mid 18th century the tradition

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:09.343
became a celebration of Easter.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.400
Although the appetizing
displays aren't edible,

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.020
a walk through the Arches of Bread

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:18.130
is a testament to the city's long history

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:21.183
and the artistic
capabilities of its citizens.

00:01:28.446 --> 00:01:31.529
(electronic dinging)

